THOUGHT: The NullAway error is due to getBasicImage dereferencing tileset.getSpritesheet(), which is annotated @Nullable. The safest minimal fix is to null-check the spritesheet before calling getSprite and return null if it’s absent, without changing other behavior. I’ll update getBasicImage accordingly and then run the Gradle compile to ensure the NullAway error count drops by one and no new errors are introduced.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/litiengine && sed -i '89,96c\  @Nullable
  @Override
  public BufferedImage getBasicImage() {
    if (this.image != null) {
      return Resources.images().get(this.image.getAbsoluteSourcePath());
    }
    final Spritesheet spritesheet = this.tileset.getSpritesheet();
    if (spritesheet == null) {
      return null;
    }
    return spritesheet.getSprite(this.getId(), this.tileset.getMargin(), this.tileset.getSpacing());
  }' src/de/gurkenlabs/litiengine/environment/tilemap/xml/TilesetEntry.java && ./gradlew compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -E "NullAway: .* errors" -n new_build_output.log || sed -n '80,110p' new_build_output.log
```

